=== file: README.md ===
# Customer review replies

This workflow asks a platform configurator to confirm setup, reads a review through the read-only `ReviewReader`, and drafts a rating-appropriate reply. Reviews rated 1–3 stars require approval from `BadReviewApprover`; every reply requires approval from `PublishApprover`.

## Configure the platform

Set `REVIEW_PLATFORM_BASE_URL` and `REVIEW_PLATFORM_TOKEN` in the runtime environment. The HTTP tools use TLS and restrict access to the declared review and reply paths. The plan did not identify a platform or provide an OpenAPI specification, so these paths are placeholders for the connected platform's API. Adapt the allowlisted paths to that platform before running against it.

## Publication safety limitation

`ReviewPublisher` is declared with a restricted write path but is intentionally not granted to `ReplyDrafter`. That agent reads untrusted review content, so giving it a publishing capability would combine untrusted input and a customer-facing write in one agent. The plan permits only one agent and lists no deterministic Java task or separate publication-only agent. Consequently, this project stops at `APPROVED_PUBLICATION_NOT_EXECUTED`; an approval is recorded as a decision in the workflow, but no platform write occurs. Do not treat approval as publication. To enable publishing, add a separately reviewed, publication-only component that receives only typed, approved values and requires approval for the write.

The workflow fails closed when configuration is not confirmed, the rating is outside 1–5, or reading/drafting fails. No failure path publishes a reply.

## Tests

Run `weave test main.loom`. The cases in `tests/main.test.yaml` script model and human responses without making network calls or platform changes.
